<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4830" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Baecŭla</span></b> , ae, f.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A small town in Spain</i>, <i>on the
				borders of Bœtica</i>, now <i>Baylen</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 27, 18, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">28, 13,
			16</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Another town in Spain</i>, <i>on the
				Ebro</i>, <i>in the territory of the
			Ausetani</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βαίκυλα</span>,
			Ptol.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Baecŭlōnenses</span></b> , ium,
				m., <i>the inhabitants of</i> Baecula,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				3, 3, 4, § 23</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
